  "body": "## What changed\n\nA boring bar's body is now judged on its cutting feeds, not only on its rapids.\n\n- New `operation/turning_feeds.rs` walks each feed of a bore op. At each station it judges the bar's head (`flute_len` above the nose) and shank (`shank_len` above that), at `turning::bar_spans` sizes. It checks them against the revolved part, and against the stock minus everything cut by then: drills ahead, turning ops ahead, the faced end, this path's earlier feeds, and this feed's own cut so far. The nose's own cut isn't judged.\n- A hit becomes `ShankHit { at, part }` and blocks the post. A move is named at most once, so moves the solid law already named are skipped.\n- `generate.rs` builds the shared `Meridian` context once for both the rapid law and the feed law. `turning_rapids.rs` helpers become `pub(super)`.\n- Behaviour change: a bore over a pilot narrower than the nose-centre radius is now flagged on its feeds.\n\n## Pins (`turning_bore`)\n\n- `a_bar_whose_head_rides_the_uncut_band_above_its_nose_is_convicted` (a Ø10 bar, Ø12 bore, Ø10.6 pilot): **fails on main**, which names only the top retract rapid\n- `a_stepped_bar_whose_shank_rubs_the_wall_during_the_ride_is_convicted`: a regression pin, already caught on main by the solid law (`part: true`)\n- `a_bored_op_runs_clean_in_the_document`: still clean\n\n## Readings\n\napp turning_bore 13, turning_axial_rapids 2, turning_contour 10, lathe_post 7, lathe_post_refusals 5, turning 5, lib 74; motion turning_bore 11, turning_contour 13, lib 126; clippy on motion and app is clean.\n\nChangelog: A boring bar's head and shank are judged on its cutting feeds against the part and the stock still uncut (pilot, ops ahead, its own cut so far); a body that rubs is a ShankHit that blocks the post\n\nFixes #146\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
